<title>USA: U.S. Aug housing starts rose 4.5 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. Aug housing starts rose 4.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce housing starts and building permits, seasonally adjusted annual rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -     --August--    ---July------Rev from--     Aug96/95</p>
<p>    -     Pct   Rate    Pct   Rate   Pct   Rate     Pct   Rate</p>
<p> Starts   4.5  1,525   -2.0  1,460  -1.3  1,455     8.9  1,401</p>
<p> Permits -4.4  1,393    3.0  1,457   2.6  1,452     1.0  1,379</p>
<p>    -     - - - - - -August Regional Breakdown- - - - - -</p>
<p>    -     Northeast    -Midwest-    --South--    --West--</p>
<p>    -     Pct  Rate    Pct  Rate    Pct  Rate    Pct  Rate</p>
<p> Starts   7.0   138   -2.0   342    2.8   667   13.5   378</p>
<p> Permits  9.6   149   -9.8   305   -0.8   620  -10.9   319</p>
<p>Seasonally Adjusted Annual Rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p> Starts:     Aug  July--Rev from  Aug95</p>
<p> -Single   1,238  1,143  1,133    1,135</p>
<p> -Multiple   287    317    322	266</p>
<p>Permits:</p>
<p> -Single   1,073  1,073  1,070    1,046</p>
<p> -Multiple   320    384    382	333</p>
<p>Unadjusted Actual Starts and Permits, in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	  Aug  July--Rev from   Aug95</p>
<p>  Starts     142    136    136	136</p>
<p>  Permits    127    136    135	134</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast August starts at a 1.445 million unit annual rate.</p>
<p>The August starts level was the highest since March 1994 when it was 1.531 million, the department said.</p>
<p>June starts were revised to a 0.8 percent rise to an annual rate of 1.490 million units. Previously, it said June starts fell 0.3 percent to a 1.474 million unit annual rate. June permits were unrevised, falling 2.5 percent to an annual rate of 1.415 million units.</p>
